edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530682 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530695 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530699 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530714 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530725 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530730 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530731 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186530732 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186535084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1039 "Express Surface Integrals as Repeated Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1040 #edb/ref 17592186530737 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186105459 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105889 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8885504f-07fb-5308-a982-608d7baa262b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186106889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1045 "Surface Integrals Over Cartesian Surfaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186106886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1050 900.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186105951 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "55efdebf-c5f4-5896-8a96-24cfe4c710eb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106064 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186278081 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106064 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161355" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106064 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106064 #edb/ref 1071 "Evaluate the surface integral \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{1+2{cos}^{2}⁡(x+y)}}\\,\\text{d}S\n$$\n\nwhere $S$ is defined by $z=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)$ for $0\\le x\\le \\pi $ and $-x\\le y\\le x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106064 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1a32ff2f-f5fc-57a4-9ce0-9a59d7c231d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106064 #edb/ref 1074 "For a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFor the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂x}=\\frac{∂}{∂x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y),\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂z}{∂y}=\\frac{∂}{∂y}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be evaluated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\frac{z}{\\sqrt{1+2{cos}^{2}⁡(x+y)}}\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(x,y,g(x,y))\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}{\\sqrt{1+2{cos}^{2}⁡(x+y)}}\\sqrt{1+2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y))^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)}{\\cancel{\\sqrt{1+2{cos}^{2}⁡(x+y)}}}\\cancel{\\sqrt{1+2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y))^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{-x}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }[-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x+y)]_{y=-x}^{y=x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x-\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)}{2}]}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1061 44418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f07960b-27be-5aa0-93a1-7182414f7f51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106886 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186107153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1061 44419 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a2865c0f-bb8c-5298-b8b6-d39fcd4dd416" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106887 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1061 44421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4324e02b-29a0-51f1-961f-3fecc2a25950" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106888 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186106887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1061 44429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "edfeb55c-dcca-540f-9b5b-f35820d75f59" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186106889 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186105889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1064 "Recall that for a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v) \\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNow, if a surface is given by the explicit equation $z=g(x,y)$ over a plane region $D$ in Cartesian coordinates, then the canonical parametrization of this surface is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(x,y) = \\langle x,\\:  y, \\: g(x,y) \\rangle, \\qquad (x,y) \\in D.\n$$\n\nMoreover, we know that under the canonical parametrization, the magnitude of the fundamental vector product is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{x}^{′}\\times {r}_{y}^{′}‖ & =\\sqrt{1+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂x})}^{2}+{(\\frac{∂z}{∂y})}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, for a surface $S$ defined by $z=g(x,y)$ with $(x,y)\\in D\\subseteq \\mathbb R^2,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f(x,y,z)$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f\\left(x,y,g(x,y)\\right) \\sqrt{1+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial x}\\right)^2+\\left(\\dfrac{\\partial z}{\\partial y}\\right)^2} \\: \\text{d}A.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1065 7650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "411ccf43-163d-53bb-b1f4-2b6832c905e1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186107153 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1080 "-6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275528 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "05c6bd5e-0a05-54b2-8760-1af815a21d72" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1080 "-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275629 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1117310d-a59f-5c9e-afac-07ea4e950362" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1080 "\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275701 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "181d1c26-e67d-51c2-a26a-430f785d6acb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275844 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "28969ccb-d093-57d3-b212-4874bada94e4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275874 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275874 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186275874 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2ba05209-d34b-5868-9786-58e2ff4e93bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276275 #edb/ref 1080 "2\\sqrt{3}-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186276275